1
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,195
We're riding towards Absolution.

2
00:03:26,737 --> 00:03:28,637
You know how far west we are?

3
00:03:37,454 --> 00:03:39,183
Maybe he's a dummy.

4
00:03:39,757 --> 00:03:42,692
Is there a reason
you're not answering my question?

5
00:03:43,463 --> 00:03:46,523
Look here, Pa.
He's got iron on his wrist.

6
00:03:46,634 --> 00:03:48,659
He's been shot.

7
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:51,261
Could be he done
broke out of the hoosegow.

8
00:03:51,374 --> 00:03:52,739
Might be worth bounty money.

9
00:03:52,843 --> 00:03:54,367
Might could be.

10
00:04:02,390 --> 00:04:04,950
It's not your lucky day, stranger.

11
00:04:06,396 --> 00:04:07,658
Turn around and start walking.

12
00:04:09,902 --> 00:04:12,063
I said turn around and start walking!

13
00:07:03,428 --> 00:07:04,725
Get out.

14
00:07:41,885 --> 00:07:43,113
Hello?

15
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:39,030
Palms to heaven, friend.

16
00:08:39,571 --> 00:08:41,368
Easy now.

17
00:08:47,750 --> 00:08:51,811
All right. Turn around, nice and slow.

18
00:08:52,290 --> 00:08:53,780
I've been shot.

19
00:09:00,670 --> 00:09:04,231
Only two kinds of men get shot,
criminals and victims.

20
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:07,577
Which one are you?

21
00:09:09,114 --> 00:09:10,342
I don't know.

22
00:09:10,818 --> 00:09:12,342
You got a name, friend?

23
00:09:13,689 --> 00:09:15,520
I don't know that either.

24
00:09:16,192 --> 00:09:17,784
Just what do you know?

25
00:09:19,130 --> 00:09:20,495
English.

26
00:09:28,111 --> 00:09:31,877
Well, that is a right odd-looking
wound there.

27
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:35,915
Looks almost cauterized.

28
00:09:36,789 --> 00:09:39,451
All right, this might sting a bit.

29
00:09:42,466 --> 00:09:43,592
Is this a mining town?

30
00:09:46,639 --> 00:09:50,268
Yeah. Well, that was the notion.

31
00:09:51,412 --> 00:09:55,348
People moved on, though. No gold.

32
00:09:55,485 --> 00:09:57,646
All right now, try and hold still.

33
00:10:01,327 --> 00:10:02,817
There we go.

34
00:10:04,264 --> 00:10:06,198
This is no gunshot.

35
00:10:06,902 --> 00:10:08,233
Where'd you get this, son?

36
00:10:08,337 --> 00:10:09,770
I don't know.

37
00:10:09,873 --> 00:10:13,900
I can't rightly absolve you of your sins
if you don't recall 'em, can I?

38
00:10:14,446 --> 00:10:18,177
That being said,
I've seen good men do bad things

39
00:10:18,285 --> 00:10:20,583
and bad men do good things.

40
00:10:21,490 --> 00:10:24,254
Whether you're gonna
end up in heaven or hell,

41
00:10:24,362 --> 00:10:26,990
it's not God's plan, it's your own.

42
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:30,428
You just got to remember what it was.

43
00:10:30,537 --> 00:10:32,471
All right, put me a finger right here.

44
00:10:32,573 --> 00:10:33,767
Come on.

45
00:10:34,409 --> 00:10:35,501
There you go.

46
00:10:39,984 --> 00:10:41,315
There.

47
00:10:42,154 --> 00:10:43,746
Thank you.

48
00:10:43,857 --> 00:10:45,825
Not bad for a country preacher.

49
00:10:52,636 --> 00:10:54,661
It's that damn fool Dolarhyde kid.

50
00:10:56,509 --> 00:10:58,409
Hey! What are you doing?

51
00:10:58,512 --> 00:11:00,605
What are you doing, Percy?
There's people up there!

52
00:11:00,716 --> 00:11:02,206
There's no one up there. It's fine.

53
00:11:02,318 --> 00:11:04,548
It's not fine.
It's bad enough he drinks for free.

54
00:11:04,655 --> 00:11:06,816
Now he's got to shoot up the place?

55
00:11:06,924 --> 00:11:08,152
Wait, what was that, Doc?

56
00:11:08,260 --> 00:11:10,228
Nothing. He didn't say anything.
Everything's okay.

57
00:11:10,330 --> 00:11:11,592
Please go back inside.

58
00:11:11,732 --> 00:11:12,824
Shut up.

59
00:11:15,004 --> 00:11:18,872
I want to hear what you said.
"It's bad enough" what?

60
00:11:20,779 --> 00:11:23,373
You ungrateful for our business?

61
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:26,011
'Cause if it wasn't for my pa's cattle,

62
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:28,213
there'd be no money
going through this town!

63
00:11:28,323 --> 00:11:32,987
There'd be no meat on your tables!
And your doors would be closed!

64
00:11:35,167 --> 00:11:37,692
I don't mean no disrespect
to your father, Percy. You know that.

65
00:11:37,805 --> 00:11:41,468
Of course not.
But you ask me to pay.

66
00:11:43,513 --> 00:11:44,605
Come here, let's settle up.

67
00:11:46,584 --> 00:11:47,846
Come here.

68
00:11:53,695 --> 00:11:54,662
Hey.

69
00:11:55,331 --> 00:11:58,129
Hey, kid, I don't want any trouble.
I'm just trying to...

70
00:12:00,271 --> 00:12:04,674
Better pick up your glasses, Doc,
before someone steps on them.

71
00:12:10,988 --> 00:12:11,955
Stop!

72
00:12:12,056 --> 00:12:13,455
I'll pay the goddamn bill!

73
00:12:13,757 --> 00:12:18,421
All right, son! We're just trying
to make a living now. Come on.

74
00:12:18,532 --> 00:12:22,263
You know what, preacher?
You just gave me an idea.

75
00:12:22,605 --> 00:12:25,096
I know it ain't Sunday, folks,

76
00:12:25,243 --> 00:12:28,735
but what say we take up
a collection for the poor man?

77
00:12:30,316 --> 00:12:32,079
Now, who's got money?

78
00:12:33,154 --> 00:12:34,519
In the hat.

79
00:12:35,824 --> 00:12:37,348
Let's go.

80
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:39,087
Much obliged.

81
00:12:39,196 --> 00:12:41,187
Now, I'm sorry Doc's bad fortune

82
00:12:41,299 --> 00:12:43,961
has to be taken out on you good people.
In the hat.

83
00:12:45,071 --> 00:12:47,005
That's mighty Christian of you.

84
00:12:51,414 --> 00:12:52,381
Hey.

85
00:12:54,719 --> 00:12:56,050
You, too.

86
00:12:56,522 --> 00:13:00,014
You want to be careful where you point
that thing before you get hurt.

87
00:13:07,572 --> 00:13:09,039
Listen...

88
00:13:10,510 --> 00:13:15,311
I'm gonna give you
the benefit of the doubt, because

89
00:13:16,351 --> 00:13:18,649
maybe you don't know who I am.

90
00:13:31,908 --> 00:13:34,069
- Come on.
- Get off of me!

91
00:13:34,179 --> 00:13:35,476
Hey, you!

92
00:13:37,683 --> 00:13:39,241
I'm warning you.

93
00:13:51,404 --> 00:13:52,962
Are you all right?

94
00:13:53,073 --> 00:13:54,563
Where the hell did he come from?

95
00:13:54,676 --> 00:13:57,543
Where the hell did he come from?

96
00:13:57,647 --> 00:13:59,638
What the hell is going on here?

97
00:14:01,052 --> 00:14:04,579
It was an accident.
He came out of nowhere.

98
00:14:04,690 --> 00:14:08,649
And he dry-gulched me.
He tried to make me look like a fool.

99
00:14:08,763 --> 00:14:10,560
It wasn't my fault, Sheriff.

100
00:14:10,666 --> 00:14:14,363
Damn it, Percy. You crossed the line
this time. I gotta lock you up.

101
00:14:14,472 --> 00:14:15,700
Taggart.

102
00:14:16,441 --> 00:14:18,705
You know that's not a good idea.

103
00:14:19,312 --> 00:14:22,304
Well, I'm afraid I got no choice, Nat.

104
00:14:24,788 --> 00:14:25,846
Nat?

105
00:14:26,623 --> 00:14:29,217
Nat, you son of a bitch,
where you going?

106
00:14:29,326 --> 00:14:34,354
Don't worry. I'll tell your father
about what happened today.

107
00:14:38,641 --> 00:14:40,836
You burned the coffee again, Mickey.

108
00:14:40,944 --> 00:14:44,175
Well. Tell you what, Ed.
Next time, you can make the coffee.

109
00:14:44,283 --> 00:14:45,375
- Okay.
- All right.

110
00:14:45,485 --> 00:14:47,885
Why don't you take it easy
on that Taos Lightnin', Murphy?

111
00:14:47,988 --> 00:14:50,115
Mr. Dolarhyde
don't like drinking on the job.

112
00:14:50,225 --> 00:14:53,626
Mr. Dolarhyde
don't like drinking on the job?

113
00:14:55,500 --> 00:15:00,460
I don't give a rat's ass what the high
and mighty Colonel Dolarhyde don't like!

114
00:15:01,171 --> 00:15:04,629
I don't care how many Indians
he put under neither.

115
00:15:04,742 --> 00:15:07,438
You sure do flap your gums a lot
when the boss ain't around.

116
00:15:12,515 --> 00:15:15,211
I'd say it to his face if he was here!

117
00:15:16,219 --> 00:15:18,187
Colonel Dolarhyde.

118
00:15:24,193 --> 00:15:27,162
I'm gonna tell you something, boys.

119
00:15:28,997 --> 00:15:31,124
Money makes you soft.

120
00:16:08,066 --> 00:16:09,693
Where the hell's that coach?

121
00:16:10,503 --> 00:16:12,232
Coach? What coach?

122
00:16:12,337 --> 00:16:14,305
You shot a deputy, Percy.

123
00:16:14,907 --> 00:16:17,398
Federal Marshal's
bringing you to Santa Fe.

124
00:16:17,508 --> 00:16:19,237
Federal Marshal?

125
00:16:19,344 --> 00:16:21,710
Sheriff, have you lost your mind?

126
00:16:22,414 --> 00:16:24,609
My pa is on his way down here.

127
00:16:24,715 --> 00:16:27,809
You better let me out of here
before things get out of hand.

128
00:16:28,519 --> 00:16:33,616
Sheriff, it was an accident!
It's not like I'm Jesse James!

129
00:16:33,857 --> 00:16:35,381
Son of a bitch.

130
00:16:37,794 --> 00:16:40,422
Could you put that on Percy's tab?

131
00:16:41,698 --> 00:16:43,325
Fifty cents.

132
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:45,658
Just kidding with you, there, Doc.

133
00:16:49,872 --> 00:16:52,170
I got no respect in this town.

134
00:16:52,274 --> 00:16:53,901
That's not true, okay?

135
00:16:55,277 --> 00:16:56,608
You want to leave?

136
00:16:56,712 --> 00:17:00,443
No. This is your dream.
I'd follow you anywhere.

137
00:17:00,549 --> 00:17:01,777
I thought it was our dream.

138
00:17:03,885 --> 00:17:05,614
God damn it!

139
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:07,915
Hey, Charlie,
why don't you play something festive?

140
00:17:08,022 --> 00:17:10,149
It's like a funeral in here!

141
00:17:16,063 --> 00:17:19,294
Hey, you don't have
to prove anything, okay?

142
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:21,630
Okay? I love you.

143
00:17:21,735 --> 00:17:23,327
I'm not a child.

144
00:17:36,816 --> 00:17:38,477
Whiskey.

145
00:17:44,322 --> 00:17:46,847
On the house, for what you did.

146
00:18:06,277 --> 00:18:08,074
I'm just here to drink.

147
00:18:13,616 --> 00:18:15,811
- Do I know you?
- No.

148
00:18:21,691 --> 00:18:23,056
My name's Ella.

149
00:18:26,295 --> 00:18:28,763
Where'd you get your bracelet?

150
00:18:30,966 --> 00:18:34,231
There something you know about me,
lady?

151
00:18:35,537 --> 00:18:37,971
You don't remember anything, do you?

152
00:18:41,643 --> 00:18:43,543
What do you want?

153
00:18:43,644 --> 00:18:46,238
I know you're looking for something.

154
00:18:46,347 --> 00:18:47,644
So am I.

155
00:18:50,484 --> 00:18:51,610
Well, good luck to you.

156
00:19:00,627 --> 00:19:01,651
Move away.

157
00:19:10,636 --> 00:19:12,263
Jake Lonergan.

158
00:19:31,888 --> 00:19:34,288
You mind following me
over to the office,

159
00:19:34,392 --> 00:19:36,326
so we can have us a little chat?

160
00:19:39,730 --> 00:19:42,028
I think you've got the wrong man.

161
00:19:44,568 --> 00:19:47,366
Well, I'm gonna need you
to come with us all the same.

162
00:19:50,906 --> 00:19:52,373
Wouldn't do that if I was you.

163
00:20:19,867 --> 00:20:21,095
No!

164
00:20:24,371 --> 00:20:26,339
I don't want any trouble.

165
00:21:09,846 --> 00:21:11,541
Rise and shine.

166
00:21:15,318 --> 00:21:17,809
You're in trouble now.

167
00:21:17,922 --> 00:21:20,049
You're gonna burn.

168
00:21:20,156 --> 00:21:22,283
My pa is coming for me.

169
00:21:23,059 --> 00:21:28,326
He learned how to kill a man
good and slow in the war.

170
00:21:28,431 --> 00:21:31,366
I am going to watch you suffer

171
00:21:31,468 --> 00:21:33,800
for a long,

172
00:21:33,902 --> 00:21:35,369
long,

173
00:21:35,471 --> 00:21:37,632
long time.

174
00:21:39,173 --> 00:21:43,473
You thought
that cheap shot in the pecker hurt?

175
00:21:51,953 --> 00:21:54,922
Please! I didn't kill your cattle.

176
00:21:55,857 --> 00:21:58,826
Colonel Dolarhyde.
You got to believe me!

177
00:22:01,294 --> 00:22:04,923
You only been riding for my brand
for what, two weeks?

178
00:22:07,134 --> 00:22:10,297
You don't maybe know
who you're dealing with, Roy.

179
00:22:14,141 --> 00:22:16,268
Nobody calls me "Colonel."

180
00:22:17,476 --> 00:22:19,876
Them that did are mostly dead.

181
00:22:23,582 --> 00:22:24,879
Please.

182
00:22:26,819 --> 00:22:30,619
So you, Ed and Little Mickey is picking
up strays. How many did you get?

183
00:22:30,989 --> 00:22:33,150
Got 24 of 'em, boss.

184
00:22:33,258 --> 00:22:35,818
You been drinking, ain't you?
I can smell it on you.

185
00:22:35,926 --> 00:22:39,054
I haven't been drinking none.
It's them other two's that drinked.

186
00:22:39,430 --> 00:22:43,730
What kind of a man goes around
blowing up other people's cows

187
00:22:43,834 --> 00:22:48,328
then tells a bullshit story like this?
You couldn't do no better?

188
00:22:48,438 --> 00:22:50,872
You got to believe me.
There was white lights!

189
00:22:51,007 --> 00:22:52,338
There was bright lights!

190
00:22:52,441 --> 00:22:56,400
So there was this big light,
and you fell in the river

191
00:22:56,512 --> 00:22:57,945
and when you come back,

192
00:22:58,047 --> 00:23:00,641
two of my best hands
has just disappeared.

193
00:23:02,951 --> 00:23:07,752
There weren't no storm.
There weren't no lightning this evening.

194
00:23:08,190 --> 00:23:09,919
You don't respect me, do you, Roy?

195
00:23:10,025 --> 00:23:11,083
Boss!

196
00:23:14,629 --> 00:23:16,392
Where's Percy?

197
00:23:16,498 --> 00:23:18,329
Taggart locked him up, boss.

198
00:23:18,433 --> 00:23:21,129
Why? What'd he do now?

199
00:23:21,535 --> 00:23:23,059
Shot a deputy.

200
00:23:23,170 --> 00:23:25,001
God damn it!

201
00:23:25,105 --> 00:23:27,938
What the hell
does Taggart think he's doing?

202
00:23:28,042 --> 00:23:30,101
He wouldn't even have a job if I...

203
00:23:30,211 --> 00:23:33,203
Now I got to go in there
and reason with him!

204
00:23:33,314 --> 00:23:36,283
'Cause you failed to look after my boy!

205
00:23:40,820 --> 00:23:42,947
Thank you. Thank you.

206
00:23:46,225 --> 00:23:47,783
All right. Everybody, saddle up.

207
00:23:52,764 --> 00:23:55,392
Boss, we ought to get more hands.

208
00:23:55,500 --> 00:23:56,558
Why?

209
00:23:57,279 --> 00:24:01,511
You're not gonna believe this,
but I think Jake Lonergan's in town.

210
00:24:12,349 --> 00:24:15,045
I'm turning you over
to the Federal Marshal.

211
00:24:17,086 --> 00:24:18,815
You're gonna tell me
what I am charged with?

212
00:24:21,523 --> 00:24:24,253
Arson. Assault.

213
00:24:24,359 --> 00:24:26,452
Mayhem. Hijacking.

214
00:24:28,763 --> 00:24:33,257
It says you robbed the stage last month
with Pat Dolan and Bull McCade.

215
00:24:33,935 --> 00:24:36,665
Which makes you
accessory to every law they broke, too.

216
00:24:43,010 --> 00:24:44,068
That it?

217
00:24:44,945 --> 00:24:46,412
Murder.

218
00:24:47,547 --> 00:24:50,846
Prostitute out of Cottonwood Grove,
next county over.

219
00:24:50,950 --> 00:24:52,918
Name of Alice Wills.

220
00:24:54,954 --> 00:24:57,218
You saying I killed this woman?

221
00:24:57,555 --> 00:24:59,318
You tell me.

222
00:25:43,597 --> 00:25:44,859
Damn.

223
00:25:48,868 --> 00:25:49,857
Give me your wrist.

224
00:25:51,137 --> 00:25:52,536
Taggart, what are you doing?

225
00:25:54,107 --> 00:25:55,131
Sheriff.

226
00:25:56,309 --> 00:25:58,777
Sheriff, this is going too far.

227
00:25:59,745 --> 00:26:01,110
I was just fooling around.

228
00:26:03,081 --> 00:26:05,140
Look, I didn't mean to hurt anybody.

229
00:26:05,584 --> 00:26:06,778
Go away.

230
00:26:06,884 --> 00:26:10,877
Listen, I'm sorry, but I had no choice.
I couldn't let you leave.

231
00:26:10,988 --> 00:26:13,013
Well, I'm leaving now.

232
00:26:13,658 --> 00:26:14,886
I need you.

233
00:26:14,991 --> 00:26:17,050
You got something to say, say it.

234
00:26:18,595 --> 00:26:21,086
I need to know where you came from.

235
00:26:22,132 --> 00:26:23,429
So do I.

236
00:26:25,968 --> 00:26:26,935
Ma'am.

237
00:26:32,941 --> 00:26:34,909
You two lovebirds have a nice trip now.

238
00:26:37,512 --> 00:26:40,481
Taggart! Taggart, let me out of here!

239
00:26:41,182 --> 00:26:42,376
Sheriff!

240
00:26:43,451 --> 00:26:44,713
Sheriff!

241
00:26:45,552 --> 00:26:46,576
What are you doing?

242
00:26:48,655 --> 00:26:50,486
You get back home. Go to bed.

243
00:26:50,591 --> 00:26:52,559
Please don't go.

244
00:26:52,658 --> 00:26:55,559
I have to, Emmett. It's my job.

245
00:26:55,895 --> 00:26:57,453
I don't like it here.

246
00:26:58,264 --> 00:27:01,233
Your pa's getting things in order.
When he does he'll send for you.

247
00:27:01,834 --> 00:27:03,131
It's been a year.

248
00:27:04,237 --> 00:27:05,636
Don't worry, he will.

249
00:27:07,572 --> 00:27:09,540
And your mom's buried here.

250
00:27:10,509 --> 00:27:12,136
You know I can't leave my little girl.

251
00:27:20,184 --> 00:27:22,311
- Taggart?
- Yeah, I see them.

252
00:27:23,187 --> 00:27:25,655
Emmett, you go inside. Now.

253
00:27:45,174 --> 00:27:47,233
I want my boy, John.

254
00:27:47,341 --> 00:27:48,467
Pa?

255
00:27:48,975 --> 00:27:50,374
Pa!

256
00:27:53,613 --> 00:27:55,103
I knew you'd come for me, Pa.

257
00:27:55,215 --> 00:27:57,376
Shut up! I'll deal with you later.

258
00:27:59,753 --> 00:28:01,380
Yeah, that's Lonergan, boss.

259
00:28:06,459 --> 00:28:09,951
That's the son of a bitch
stole my gold off the bullion coach.

260
00:28:10,061 --> 00:28:11,426
I want that man.

261
00:28:11,529 --> 00:28:13,963
You're gonna have to take it up
with the judge in Santa Fe.

262
00:28:14,065 --> 00:28:15,828
I ain't going to Santa Fe.

263
00:28:15,934 --> 00:28:17,868
You give him to me now

264
00:28:17,969 --> 00:28:19,698
or I'm gonna take him.

265
00:28:19,803 --> 00:28:21,134
What about me, Pa?

266
00:28:21,238 --> 00:28:22,899
I said, shut up, boy!

267
00:29:01,641 --> 00:29:03,199
What the hell is that?

268
00:29:23,127 --> 00:29:24,754
What the hell?

269
00:29:45,847 --> 00:29:46,814
Hey!

270
00:30:08,801 --> 00:30:10,291
- They're coming back!
- They're coming around again.

271
00:30:10,403 --> 00:30:12,030
They're coming back! Dismount!

272
00:30:24,416 --> 00:30:25,405
- Get out of the way!
- Maria!

273
00:30:25,817 --> 00:30:27,114
Oh, God!

274
00:30:27,618 --> 00:30:29,108
Don't move! Don't move!

275
00:30:29,219 --> 00:30:31,949
Stay there! Stay right there!
Don't move! I'm coming!

276
00:30:42,332 --> 00:30:43,765
Give me your hand.

277
00:30:43,866 --> 00:30:45,561
- Give me your hand.
- What the hell for?

278
00:30:45,667 --> 00:30:48,329
I can get us free.
Just give me your hand.

279
00:30:49,238 --> 00:30:50,535
Hold still.

280
00:30:59,981 --> 00:31:01,278
Emmett!

281
00:31:03,851 --> 00:31:04,840
Grandpa!

282
00:31:07,621 --> 00:31:08,610
Emmett!

283
00:31:09,456 --> 00:31:10,923
Emmett, it's all right. I got you, son.

284
00:31:18,030 --> 00:31:20,055
- Give me your hand.
- No!

285
00:31:20,165 --> 00:31:22,190
Come on, kid. Give me your hand!

286
00:31:37,881 --> 00:31:39,439
What is that?

287
00:32:07,474 --> 00:32:10,307
Come on, get up, boss.
Come on, we got to get out of here.

288
00:32:10,711 --> 00:32:11,837
Where's Percy?

289
00:32:15,648 --> 00:32:16,740
Come on out of there!

290
00:32:17,750 --> 00:32:20,480
- I can't, Pa.
- You can't? Coward!

291
00:32:21,453 --> 00:32:24,581
He broke my fingers!

292
00:32:30,028 --> 00:32:31,154
Pa!

293
00:32:31,696 --> 00:32:32,890
Pa!

294
00:32:35,199 --> 00:32:36,928
Let's go! We got to go!

295
00:32:38,868 --> 00:32:40,165
This way!

296
00:34:37,441 --> 00:34:40,376
- What is that thing?
- Why are you asking me?

297
00:34:40,478 --> 00:34:42,275
Because you shot it!

298
00:34:43,281 --> 00:34:44,714
With that thing.
Where'd you get that thing?

299
00:34:44,816 --> 00:34:47,080
I don't know.

300
00:34:48,118 --> 00:34:50,780
What do you mean, you don't know?

301
00:34:56,325 --> 00:34:58,350
What the hell is that?

302
00:35:00,296 --> 00:35:01,923
They took my wife.

303
00:35:05,967 --> 00:35:07,457
Hey.

304
00:35:07,569 --> 00:35:09,059
Is anyone in there?

305
00:35:10,471 --> 00:35:11,597
No.

306
00:35:11,706 --> 00:35:13,173
Is my wife in there?

307
00:35:13,274 --> 00:35:14,571
No!

308
00:35:14,675 --> 00:35:16,302
Is it dead?

309
00:35:25,786 --> 00:35:28,584
- Is it demons?
- Demons?

310
00:35:28,721 --> 00:35:31,713
I can't rightly say.
Sure does fit the description, but...

311
00:35:31,824 --> 00:35:33,815
Demons? What are you talking about?

312
00:35:33,926 --> 00:35:35,484
You talking about Bible stuff? Demons?

313
00:35:35,594 --> 00:35:37,892
- I'm not talking about anything.
- What the hell are you talking about?

314
00:35:37,996 --> 00:35:39,054
You got to calm down, Doc.

315
00:35:39,164 --> 00:35:40,153
- Calm down?
- You're scaring the boy.

316
00:35:40,265 --> 00:35:42,495
You're telling me a bunch of demons
took my wife.

317
00:35:42,601 --> 00:35:44,501
- I didn't say any such thing.
- Took our people!

318
00:35:44,602 --> 00:35:46,160
- Get a hold of yourself.
- You're telling me to calm down!

319
00:36:09,157 --> 00:36:10,954
Boss!

320
00:36:11,059 --> 00:36:12,720
Boss!

321
00:36:12,828 --> 00:36:14,386
It went this way.

322
00:36:18,099 --> 00:36:21,125
I don't know what it is, but it's bleeding.

323
00:36:23,604 --> 00:36:27,335
That's the same direction
those machines went with our kin.

324
00:36:27,841 --> 00:36:31,140
We ain't gonna be able to track it
in the dark.

325
00:36:32,512 --> 00:36:34,343
Round up the horses,
get some supplies!

326
00:36:34,446 --> 00:36:36,277
We'll set off at first light!

327
00:36:37,483 --> 00:36:38,609
You.

328
00:36:40,352 --> 00:36:42,320
You're going with us.

329
00:36:43,021 --> 00:36:47,981
I need that weapon. It's the only thing
that counts. And I figure you owe me.

330
00:36:49,627 --> 00:36:51,754
I don't see it that way.

331
00:38:02,459 --> 00:38:03,926
What do you want?

332
00:38:04,594 --> 00:38:06,255
What do you want?

333
00:38:07,364 --> 00:38:09,764
You come clean right now, or I'll kill you.

334
00:38:09,865 --> 00:38:13,892
They took my people, too.
I've been looking for them a long time.

335
00:38:14,770 --> 00:38:16,328
I know you can help me find them.

336
00:38:19,941 --> 00:38:21,841
You stay away from me.

337
00:38:32,452 --> 00:38:34,249
I can help you!

338
00:38:42,562 --> 00:38:44,393
It's heading north.

339
00:38:45,530 --> 00:38:47,657
Its tracks are still fresh.

340
00:39:00,377 --> 00:39:02,607
If it's all the same,
I'd like to ride along, too.

341
00:39:02,713 --> 00:39:04,044
Yes, ma'am.

342
00:39:05,716 --> 00:39:08,344
Got a kid and a dog, why not a woman?

343
00:39:54,860 --> 00:39:56,225
You're back.

344
00:40:12,375 --> 00:40:13,672
What's that?

345
00:40:30,525 --> 00:40:32,220
You have to take it back.

346
00:40:32,527 --> 00:40:34,051
Like hell I will.

347
00:40:34,461 --> 00:40:35,758
That's blood money.

348
00:40:35,863 --> 00:40:38,593
- Well, I goddamned earned it.
- By robbing and killing.

349
00:40:38,699 --> 00:40:40,758
That's gonna get us what we need!

350
00:41:13,163 --> 00:41:14,630
- Jake!
- Stay there!

351
00:41:14,731 --> 00:41:15,925
Jake!

352
00:41:48,127 --> 00:41:49,992
Well, well, well.

353
00:41:50,096 --> 00:41:51,893
Look who's back.

354
00:41:52,399 --> 00:41:55,163
I see you, but I don't see my gold.

355
00:41:55,267 --> 00:41:58,361
Let's say we find those people first,

356
00:41:58,469 --> 00:42:00,630
and then you can take your best shot
at collecting.

357
00:42:00,738 --> 00:42:05,038
Maybe that reward on your head
would be a more attractive proposition.

358
00:42:05,143 --> 00:42:09,773
Or I could just shoot you in the chest
and cut that thing off your arm.

359
00:42:10,715 --> 00:42:14,151
You know, Doc,
I don't even know why we're doing this.

360
00:42:14,251 --> 00:42:16,242
You know they're all dead.

361
00:42:17,420 --> 00:42:20,617
Well, I think if they wanted to kill them,
I think they would have.

362
00:42:20,724 --> 00:42:24,751
Only if the boss is right
and they was roping them.

363
00:42:25,595 --> 00:42:27,085
Bet it's to eat them.

364
00:42:28,864 --> 00:42:31,628
If it was me, I'd start with your wife.

365
00:42:34,102 --> 00:42:36,764
You gonna be like this the whole trip?
'Cause if you are,

366
00:42:36,871 --> 00:42:39,669
we ain't gonna have
too many long conversations, are we?

367
00:42:39,774 --> 00:42:42,334
Why don't you sing a song
or something?

368
00:42:42,443 --> 00:42:45,071
Cook some beans.
Do something useful.

369
00:42:54,787 --> 00:42:56,982
Take some friendly advice?

370
00:42:58,223 --> 00:43:01,283
Get yourself a gun
and learn how to use it.

371
00:43:09,367 --> 00:43:11,494
The tracks are washed away.

372
00:43:41,396 --> 00:43:46,000
I don't know much about boats,
but I'd say that one's upside-down.

373
00:43:47,167 --> 00:43:51,331
We're 500 miles from any river
big enough to hold it.

374
00:43:51,438 --> 00:43:53,736
Well, let's get inside, get out of the rain!

375
00:43:53,839 --> 00:43:55,670
I'm not going anywhere near that thing.

376
00:43:55,776 --> 00:43:58,244
Suit yourself. Sleep in the rain.

377
00:44:29,038 --> 00:44:31,131
You fixin' to say something?

378
00:44:32,507 --> 00:44:33,804
Maybe...

379
00:44:34,710 --> 00:44:37,110
Maybe we should have
called in the Army?

380
00:44:37,212 --> 00:44:39,703
I ain't gonna turn this over
to no West Pointers

381
00:44:39,815 --> 00:44:44,184
who got to get on the telegraph to ask
Washington which hand to wipe with.

382
00:44:44,285 --> 00:44:47,880
I waited around at Antietam
for 'em to tell me what to do.

383
00:44:49,790 --> 00:44:52,418
And lost 328 men

384
00:44:53,227 --> 00:44:55,024
over a cornfield.

385
00:44:56,563 --> 00:44:58,861
I remember those stories.

386
00:45:01,901 --> 00:45:04,699
I don't recollect telling you any stories.

387
00:45:05,637 --> 00:45:09,596
I'd listen when you'd tell them to Percy.

388
00:45:10,441 --> 00:45:14,070
You get this through
your thick Indian skull.

389
00:45:16,447 --> 00:45:18,847
Them stories weren't for you.

390
00:45:21,552 --> 00:45:23,577
They were for my son.

391
00:45:26,990 --> 00:45:32,189
Get out of here.
Go look after the horses. Do your job.

392
00:46:11,329 --> 00:46:14,264
You've been looking at this knife.
You like this knife?

393
00:46:28,012 --> 00:46:29,809
You look after that.

394
00:46:32,016 --> 00:46:33,313
Don't lose it.

395
00:46:42,358 --> 00:46:45,259
Don't yank on it, it's not your pecker.
Now, here.

396
00:46:45,360 --> 00:46:48,261
You're holding onto this thing
like you're hanging from it.

397
00:46:53,034 --> 00:46:55,161
What the hell am I doing?

398
00:46:57,605 --> 00:46:59,300
It's my fault she got took.

399
00:46:59,406 --> 00:47:01,067
I never should have
taken her to that town.

400
00:47:01,209 --> 00:47:03,143
No, no, no. Not your fault.

401
00:47:03,243 --> 00:47:05,677
You'll get her back.
You're setting things right.

402
00:47:05,779 --> 00:47:07,508
Just got to have faith. That's all.

403
00:47:07,614 --> 00:47:11,345
Faith. Yeah.
God's been real swell to me.

404
00:47:11,451 --> 00:47:13,112
I don't mean no disrespect, preacher,

405
00:47:13,219 --> 00:47:16,746
but either he ain't up there,
or he don't like me very much.

406
00:47:16,855 --> 00:47:20,586
Surely you don't expect the Lord
to do everything for you, do you, Doc?

407
00:47:22,126 --> 00:47:24,526
You got to earn his presence.

408
00:47:24,629 --> 00:47:28,190
Then you got to recognize it,
and then you have to act on it.

409
00:47:30,067 --> 00:47:31,534
Now, keep your eye on the target.

410
00:47:33,804 --> 00:47:35,101
And shoot.

411
00:47:41,310 --> 00:47:45,041
That's better. Better.
Come on. Let's reload.

412
00:48:07,001 --> 00:48:08,798
You been there long?

413
00:48:09,303 --> 00:48:10,600
Yes.

414
00:48:21,513 --> 00:48:23,140
There something you need?

415
00:48:24,015 --> 00:48:25,482
Who is she?

416
00:48:28,854 --> 00:48:31,254
She's the only one who knows who I am.

417
00:48:31,355 --> 00:48:33,482
No, you know who you are.

418
00:48:34,190 --> 00:48:36,818
- You just have to remember.
- Well, I can't.

419
00:48:36,928 --> 00:48:38,555
Yes, you can.

420
00:48:54,209 --> 00:48:55,676
Does it hurt?

421
00:48:59,213 --> 00:49:00,908
It's fine.

422
00:49:08,555 --> 00:49:09,681
It's here.

423
00:49:48,224 --> 00:49:50,488
Easy, hey! Easy!

424
00:49:50,593 --> 00:49:51,992
What's wrong, boy?

425
00:49:52,729 --> 00:49:54,196
Hello?

426
00:51:21,708 --> 00:51:23,471
Get away from that boy!

427
00:51:27,714 --> 00:51:28,681
No!

428
00:51:57,040 --> 00:52:00,567
- The boy. The boy.
- He's fine. He's fine.

429
00:52:01,343 --> 00:52:03,140
It's okay. It's okay.

430
00:52:06,915 --> 00:52:09,543
You go get our people back.

431
00:52:11,586 --> 00:52:14,111
God don't care who you were, son.

432
00:52:14,689 --> 00:52:16,748
Only who you are.

433
00:52:46,283 --> 00:52:47,580
Dog?

434
00:52:48,887 --> 00:52:49,979
Come on, boy!

435
00:52:52,389 --> 00:52:54,084
Where are you?

436
00:52:56,059 --> 00:52:59,392
Tracks are good. It's headed north.
Where's the men?

437
00:52:59,495 --> 00:53:02,225
They run off. Goddamn cowards.

438
00:53:02,331 --> 00:53:03,889
I can't find the dog.

439
00:53:04,000 --> 00:53:07,663
We ain't waiting for him.
He's run off or dead. Let's go.

440
00:53:07,770 --> 00:53:08,964
Hey. Hey. Wait.

441
00:53:09,070 --> 00:53:11,561
Aren't we gonna
say some words over him?

442
00:53:11,673 --> 00:53:14,733
Only one who knows what to say
is in the ground.

443
00:53:14,842 --> 00:53:17,242
Ain't it enough we took the time
to put him there?

444
00:53:17,345 --> 00:53:19,540
No. No, it's not enough.

445
00:53:31,456 --> 00:53:33,083
You go ahead.

446
00:53:37,462 --> 00:53:38,759
Lord...

447
00:53:41,800 --> 00:53:45,793
If there is such a thing as a soul
this man had a good one.

448
00:53:45,938 --> 00:53:47,030
Please protect it.

449
00:53:47,772 --> 00:53:49,399
Made me feel better.

450
00:53:49,507 --> 00:53:51,873
World was a better place
for having him.

451
00:53:51,975 --> 00:53:54,637
Dust to dust, amen. How was that?

452
00:53:54,745 --> 00:53:56,144
Good words.

453
00:54:06,822 --> 00:54:09,256
What are you all choked up about?

454
00:54:11,160 --> 00:54:13,560
I'm worried about my grandpa.

455
00:54:18,499 --> 00:54:22,902
Look. When I was only just
a little bit older than you are now

456
00:54:23,004 --> 00:54:25,131
all this was Mexico.

457
00:54:26,707 --> 00:54:32,009
Word come that the Apaches was riding
towards a settlement called Arivaca.

458
00:54:34,114 --> 00:54:35,979
My father wanted me to be a man,

459
00:54:36,082 --> 00:54:39,848
so he made me ride out with
the garrison, banging on a drum.

460
00:54:42,288 --> 00:54:44,256
Boy, was I scared.

461
00:54:47,125 --> 00:54:49,719
Well, we got there, it was too late.
They were all dead,

462
00:54:49,828 --> 00:54:52,023
the place was all burnt down.

463
00:54:52,998 --> 00:54:55,296
This one settler fella

464
00:54:56,167 --> 00:54:59,136
came crawling out of a burning cabin.

465
00:55:00,838 --> 00:55:02,305
He was bad.

466
00:55:03,274 --> 00:55:05,367
He knew he was gonna die.

467
00:55:06,509 --> 00:55:08,238
Burnt bad.

468
00:55:10,613 --> 00:55:12,240
He rolled over,

469
00:55:13,215 --> 00:55:15,342
looked up into my eyes,

470
00:55:16,685 --> 00:55:18,983
and he said, "Kill me."

471
00:55:21,856 --> 00:55:23,517
What did you do?

472
00:55:28,863 --> 00:55:31,457
I took this knife off his belt

473
00:55:32,198 --> 00:55:34,166
and I slit his throat.

474
00:55:36,636 --> 00:55:37,933
Take it.

475
00:55:41,707 --> 00:55:43,299
Be a man.

476
00:55:52,384 --> 00:55:54,682
That's a little rough, isn't it?

477
00:55:55,486 --> 00:55:57,113
He means well.

478
00:56:11,834 --> 00:56:15,395
I got him.
The tracks are closer together.

479
00:56:15,504 --> 00:56:17,438
He's slowing down,
headed to that canyon.

480
00:56:39,525 --> 00:56:41,755
Put your hands up in the air!

481
00:56:44,364 --> 00:56:46,924
That means you, too, pretty lady.

482
00:56:48,800 --> 00:56:51,200
This is what they call a hold-up.

483
00:56:51,303 --> 00:56:54,830
Welcome, everybody. Welcome.

484
00:56:58,877 --> 00:56:59,935
Boss?

485
00:57:01,545 --> 00:57:03,172
Boss, is that you?

486
00:57:04,715 --> 00:57:06,307
Lonergan?

487
00:57:06,717 --> 00:57:09,277
What in the hell are you doing here?

488
00:57:13,056 --> 00:57:15,786
Who are your <i>amigos</i>?

489
00:57:18,060 --> 00:57:20,460
Is this your new gang, Jake?

490
00:57:24,066 --> 00:57:26,626
I never thought I'd see you again, Jake.

491
00:57:29,570 --> 00:57:31,162
You were always my favorite.

492
00:57:32,206 --> 00:57:33,400
Shut up.

493
00:57:35,643 --> 00:57:36,871
Damn it.

494
00:57:36,977 --> 00:57:39,810
Jake? Did you break my tooth?

495
00:57:39,913 --> 00:57:42,211
Would you shut up? I'm thinking.

496
00:57:45,818 --> 00:57:47,979
How many boys we got left?

497
00:57:49,321 --> 00:57:50,754
About the same.

498
00:57:52,391 --> 00:57:53,790
Which is?

499
00:57:55,027 --> 00:57:56,187
Thirty?

500
00:57:56,928 --> 00:57:59,226
That's right. Thirty.

501
00:57:59,731 --> 00:58:00,823
Good.

502
00:58:02,934 --> 00:58:04,629
- That's good.
- Yeah.

503
00:58:05,937 --> 00:58:07,837
You're gonna bring me to the camp.

504
00:58:10,274 --> 00:58:12,265
It's time to set things straight.

505
00:58:14,611 --> 00:58:16,841
We're gonna go to the camp!

506
00:58:17,280 --> 00:58:18,747
How's the haul?

507
00:58:18,848 --> 00:58:22,113
Vulture Mine gold. Looking pretty rich.

508
00:58:22,217 --> 00:58:25,675
- How much dynamite we get?
- We got 50 sticks or so.

509
00:58:25,788 --> 00:58:27,449
Dolan!

510
00:58:30,859 --> 00:58:33,089
About time you got back.

511
00:58:33,194 --> 00:58:34,718
What the hell happened to you?

512
00:58:35,362 --> 00:58:36,659
He did.

513
00:58:44,170 --> 00:58:45,899
Well, shit.

514
00:58:49,909 --> 00:58:51,706
You got some balls

515
00:58:51,811 --> 00:58:54,939
riding back in here
like nothing ever happened.

516
00:58:56,014 --> 00:59:00,075
Boys! Grab your guns. We're riding out.

517
00:59:00,619 --> 00:59:02,587
Boys aren't going anywhere with you,
Jake.

518
00:59:04,522 --> 00:59:07,252
We're fixing to rob us a coach.

519
00:59:07,359 --> 00:59:08,986
And that's exactly what we're gonna do.

520
00:59:16,957 --> 00:59:18,720
Are you her?

521
00:59:19,527 --> 00:59:20,960
Am I who?

522
00:59:21,062 --> 00:59:23,792
The whore that Jake quit this gang for.

523
00:59:25,331 --> 00:59:26,559
You watch your mouth.

524
00:59:26,666 --> 00:59:27,963
Or what?

525
00:59:28,968 --> 00:59:31,698
I run this outfit now.

526
00:59:31,805 --> 00:59:33,238
Put your guns on the whore!

527
00:59:33,338 --> 00:59:37,297
If he so much as twitches,
blow her brains out of her ear.

528
00:59:40,712 --> 00:59:42,680
He said the whore.

529
00:59:44,315 --> 00:59:48,046
You call her a whore again,
it'll be the last word you ever say.

530
00:59:48,152 --> 00:59:51,451
You ain't in no position
to make threats, boyo.

531
00:59:51,556 --> 00:59:53,353
Hunt, take his gun.

532
00:59:54,324 --> 00:59:55,848
Take his gun!

533
00:59:57,561 --> 00:59:59,188
Sorry, Jake.

534
01:00:18,713 --> 01:00:20,738
Where's our gold, Jake?

535
01:00:22,049 --> 01:00:23,710
I don't remember.

536
01:00:31,757 --> 01:00:33,657
Well, I do remember

537
01:00:33,759 --> 01:00:38,059
you telling us you was leaving us
high and dry because of some woman.

538
01:00:49,073 --> 01:00:54,340
I guess you just left out the part about
taking all of our gold from that last job?

539
01:00:55,880 --> 01:00:58,348
So I'm gonna ask you one last time.

540
01:00:59,282 --> 01:01:01,375
Where is it, Jake?

541
01:01:03,720 --> 01:01:05,017
Demons.

542
01:01:08,123 --> 01:01:09,215
What's that?

543
01:01:09,792 --> 01:01:11,760
Demons took your gold.

544
01:01:12,962 --> 01:01:14,930
When you get to hell

545
01:01:16,131 --> 01:01:18,190
you can ask for it back.

546
01:01:27,308 --> 01:01:28,935
Kill the whore.

547
01:01:42,723 --> 01:01:45,453
I told you not to call her that.

548
01:01:45,614 --> 01:01:47,445
Everybody!

549
01:01:47,589 --> 01:01:48,886
Drop 'em!

550
01:01:50,174 --> 01:01:51,471
I said drop 'em!

551
01:01:59,295 --> 01:02:00,762
Not fun, is it?

552
01:02:01,337 --> 01:02:03,931
You know, that wasn't very nice.

553
01:02:08,313 --> 01:02:09,473
On your horses!

554
01:02:10,184 --> 01:02:11,242
Go!

555
01:02:12,464 --> 01:02:15,592
Jake, Jake, Jake. Don't forget your gun.

556
01:02:15,765 --> 01:02:17,027
You'll always be my favorite.

557
01:02:27,062 --> 01:02:29,155
- Mount up!
- Ride!

558
01:02:58,912 --> 01:03:01,073
- They're here!
- Move out!

559
01:03:20,964 --> 01:03:22,261
Come on!

560
01:04:34,976 --> 01:04:36,170
Okay. I got you!

561
01:04:36,302 --> 01:04:37,394
I got you!

562
01:04:53,522 --> 01:04:54,989
Can you swim?

563
01:05:00,395 --> 01:05:01,657
Oh, God.

564
01:05:01,790 --> 01:05:02,882
Turn your head!

565
01:05:19,700 --> 01:05:21,258
You all right?

566
01:05:26,369 --> 01:05:27,893
Let's get in.

567
01:05:47,978 --> 01:05:49,605
We were flying.

568
01:05:50,972 --> 01:05:52,530
Yeah!

569
01:05:52,979 --> 01:05:54,810
I don't want to do that again.

570
01:05:54,954 --> 01:05:56,080
No.

571
01:07:10,190 --> 01:07:11,384
Hey.

572
01:07:12,267 --> 01:07:14,132
Hey, you stay with me.

573
01:07:15,500 --> 01:07:16,967
Keep talking.

574
01:07:18,527 --> 01:07:20,757
You remember now, don't you?

575
01:07:22,305 --> 01:07:23,431
What?

576
01:07:24,176 --> 01:07:25,473
The woman.

577
01:07:27,239 --> 01:07:29,036
Did you love her?

578
01:07:30,643 --> 01:07:32,543
You can tell me.

579
01:07:32,684 --> 01:07:34,675
I can't remember.

580
01:07:35,405 --> 01:07:36,872
I must've.

581
01:07:37,856 --> 01:07:40,154
All I know is I owe it to her

582
01:07:41,395 --> 01:07:42,862
to find her.

583
01:07:45,309 --> 01:07:47,869
Watch out. I'm sorry.

584
01:07:48,030 --> 01:07:49,327
I'm sorry.

585
01:07:50,923 --> 01:07:52,288
I got you.

586
01:07:53,305 --> 01:07:54,772
I got you.

587
01:07:59,260 --> 01:08:00,887
It's not far now.

588
01:08:03,106 --> 01:08:04,403
You and me,

589
01:08:05,896 --> 01:08:07,693
we're gonna be just fine.

590
01:08:15,628 --> 01:08:16,595
Is that...

591
01:08:17,192 --> 01:08:18,659
Is that them?

592
01:08:19,506 --> 01:08:20,632
Boss?

593
01:08:30,736 --> 01:08:33,967
- I got her.
- Give her to me, Nat. Bring her here.

594
01:08:38,012 --> 01:08:41,880
- Here. Drink.
- No. Give it to her. Give it to her.

595
01:08:52,497 --> 01:08:54,294
Doc?

596
01:09:05,280 --> 01:09:06,770
How is she?

597
01:09:09,285 --> 01:09:11,082
She's gone, pal.

598
01:09:11,187 --> 01:09:15,749
No. No, she's not gone.

599
01:09:15,859 --> 01:09:17,952
She's not. She's not gone!

600
01:09:18,963 --> 01:09:20,260
Jake.

601
01:09:21,532 --> 01:09:23,227
She's gone.

602
01:09:57,844 --> 01:09:59,641
- Doc!
- Don't touch him!

603
01:10:00,114 --> 01:10:01,376
Doc!

604
01:10:37,061 --> 01:10:38,551
This is Black Knife.

605
01:10:40,665 --> 01:10:41,825
The last of his people.

606
01:10:41,934 --> 01:10:44,869
There's no reasoning with them.
We're all gonna die anyway.

607
01:10:44,971 --> 01:10:46,768
This is what's left of the Chiricahuas.

608
01:10:46,873 --> 01:10:47,999
Good riddance to 'em!

609
01:10:49,242 --> 01:10:51,301
He's saying the white people,

610
01:10:51,412 --> 01:10:53,243
they brought all this evil to his people.

611
01:10:53,347 --> 01:10:56,976
We brought evil? Evil was here!
You're the evil one!

612
01:10:57,119 --> 01:10:59,485
He's saying we brought the monsters.

613
01:10:59,622 --> 01:11:02,420
We didn't bring the monsters.
Tell him they took our people, too!

614
01:11:02,526 --> 01:11:03,959
Tell him they took my wife!

615
01:11:04,061 --> 01:11:06,495
Shut up!
There's no reasoning with them!

616
01:11:07,132 --> 01:11:08,656
Tell him what I said, Nat!

617
01:11:08,867 --> 01:11:10,129
Kill us now!

618
01:12:15,817 --> 01:12:18,615
I'm sorry, but I couldn't tell you.

619
01:12:18,721 --> 01:12:20,245
Are you one of them?

620
01:12:20,357 --> 01:12:23,849
No. I'm from a different place.

621
01:12:23,961 --> 01:12:27,021
I took this form
so I could walk among you.

622
01:12:28,366 --> 01:12:29,890
You should have told me.

623
01:12:30,002 --> 01:12:32,596
I didn't know if I could heal this body,

624
01:12:32,705 --> 01:12:34,434
if I would wake up.

625
01:12:46,288 --> 01:12:48,779
He wants to know where you're from.

626
01:12:58,604 --> 01:12:59,696
What'd she say?

627
01:12:59,804 --> 01:13:03,137
She says she came from a place
above the stars.

628
01:13:03,610 --> 01:13:05,908
What does that mean? Another world?
What do you mean?

629
01:13:06,013 --> 01:13:07,981
What does that mean? What?

630
01:13:08,283 --> 01:13:10,080
He says you shouldn't talk.

631
01:13:10,185 --> 01:13:11,709
What do you mean I shouldn't talk?
I got questions...

632
01:13:12,821 --> 01:13:14,186
You're a guest of the chief.

633
01:13:14,291 --> 01:13:17,089
Now I'm a guest? I thought
I was a prisoner! What the hell am I?

634
01:13:17,193 --> 01:13:19,855
Enough! All right. You're both big men!
Great warriors!

635
01:13:19,964 --> 01:13:22,455
Can we just listen to the woman
tell her story?

636
01:13:22,566 --> 01:13:24,295
Or whatever she is?
What are they doing here?

637
01:13:24,670 --> 01:13:26,194
They want gold.

638
01:13:28,608 --> 01:13:30,098
Well, that's just ridiculous.

639
01:13:30,210 --> 01:13:32,337
What are they gonna do,
buy something?

640
01:13:32,446 --> 01:13:35,142
It's as rare to them as it is to you.

641
01:13:35,249 --> 01:13:36,341
What about my grandpa?

642
01:13:36,451 --> 01:13:40,717
What about my wife? What about
the other people? Are they still alive?

643
01:13:40,823 --> 01:13:42,814
If they are, they won't be for long.

644
01:13:44,929 --> 01:13:47,227
They're studying your weaknesses.

645
01:13:47,332 --> 01:13:49,300
These are just scouts.

646
01:13:49,400 --> 01:13:54,497
If we let them leave, they'll come back
with more and there will be no survivors.

647
01:13:54,819 --> 01:13:56,946
That's what they did to my people.

648
01:13:56,945 --> 01:13:59,573
I came here to make sure
it would not happen again,

649
01:13:59,583 --> 01:14:02,108
but we have to work together.

650
01:14:08,264 --> 01:14:10,494
He says his people will join her.

651
01:14:11,203 --> 01:14:12,170
What do you mean, join her?

652
01:14:12,270 --> 01:14:14,170
What's she going to do?
Where you going to go?

653
01:14:14,274 --> 01:14:16,139
We can find them.
He knows where they are.

654
01:14:20,618 --> 01:14:21,710
No, I don't.

655
01:14:23,389 --> 01:14:26,256
I can't remember anything.
I couldn't even remember my own name.

656
01:14:30,067 --> 01:14:32,797
He says they will take care of that.

657
01:16:57,873 --> 01:16:59,670
I brought the gold.

658
01:17:00,944 --> 01:17:02,275
Into the house.

659
01:17:04,049 --> 01:17:06,313
That's why she died.

660
01:17:07,088 --> 01:17:09,283
It's not your fault.

661
01:18:19,037 --> 01:18:20,937
I know where they are.

662
01:19:07,350 --> 01:19:09,477
Jesus, Mary and Joseph.

663
01:19:11,423 --> 01:19:13,482
How did they build something like that?

664
01:19:13,627 --> 01:19:16,425
They arrived in it. It's their vessel.

665
01:19:16,931 --> 01:19:19,229
That's only the top.
The rest is underground.

666
01:19:19,336 --> 01:19:20,564
It's how they mine for gold.

667
01:19:20,671 --> 01:19:22,298
So there is gold here.

668
01:19:23,443 --> 01:19:24,967
Can they see out of there?

669
01:19:25,446 --> 01:19:27,107
They don't see well in daylight.

670
01:19:27,215 --> 01:19:29,945
They stay underground in caverns
where it's dark.

671
01:20:00,571 --> 01:20:02,198
We'll never even get close.

672
01:20:02,339 --> 01:20:04,273
Those flying machines
will just pick us off

673
01:20:04,375 --> 01:20:05,740
before we get anywhere near it.

674
01:20:05,844 --> 01:20:07,709
There is another way in.

675
01:20:08,516 --> 01:20:09,983
Down there.

676
01:20:10,752 --> 01:20:12,185
The way I came out.

677
01:20:14,092 --> 01:20:15,855
We got to get those creatures
out of there

678
01:20:15,962 --> 01:20:19,329
and out in the open,
where we can get at them.

679
01:20:19,433 --> 01:20:22,596
So you can get in with that arm gun,
get our people out.

680
01:20:24,542 --> 01:20:27,670
We have one advantage,
they underestimate you.

681
01:20:27,780 --> 01:20:29,680
You're like insects to them.

682
01:20:29,784 --> 01:20:32,582
They're not planning on defending
themselves, so they'll be vulnerable.

683
01:20:33,890 --> 01:20:37,451
- We haven't got enough men.
- This ain't gonna work.

684
01:20:42,004 --> 01:20:44,973
He says he wants to use your spyglass.

685
01:21:11,217 --> 01:21:14,118
The Apaches are mountain warriors.

686
01:21:14,222 --> 01:21:18,022
He says it's better to fight
from high ground.

687
01:21:19,230 --> 01:21:20,663
Tell him he's a fool.

688
01:21:20,766 --> 01:21:23,735
There is no high ground
while they got those flying machines.

689
01:21:24,238 --> 01:21:25,500
Jake's leaving!

690
01:21:33,220 --> 01:21:34,653
That's just dandy.

691
01:21:34,789 --> 01:21:36,916
Son of a bitch.

692
01:21:39,864 --> 01:21:41,798
Quit stalling.
How much gold we had left?

693
01:21:42,100 --> 01:21:44,660
Barely enough.
But I'm gonna need my share right now

694
01:21:44,661 --> 01:21:47,061
so I can get as far away from here
as I possibly can.

695
01:21:50,054 --> 01:21:52,852
- Red?
- I got him, Bull.

696
01:21:55,031 --> 01:21:56,658
Hey, there.

697
01:21:59,275 --> 01:22:02,267
I had one hell of a job finding you boys.

698
01:22:03,952 --> 01:22:05,852
You planning a trip?

699
01:22:08,797 --> 01:22:10,924
We're going as far away as we can go.

700
01:22:11,035 --> 01:22:12,969
You remember <i>la playa</i>
in Puerto Vallarta?

701
01:22:13,072 --> 01:22:14,664
They got good fishing.

702
01:22:15,411 --> 01:22:17,971
Good tequila.
You want to come with us?

703
01:22:18,083 --> 01:22:20,278
Don't make no difference.

704
01:22:21,492 --> 01:22:23,221
It's not far enough.

705
01:22:25,334 --> 01:22:27,598
What in the hell
were those things, Jake?

706
01:22:27,706 --> 01:22:29,401
It doesn't matter.

707
01:22:29,510 --> 01:22:33,640
They're gonna find us
and they're gonna wipe us out.

708
01:22:34,454 --> 01:22:36,547
What in the hell are you saying?

709
01:22:37,461 --> 01:22:40,055
What I'm saying is you got a choice.

710
01:22:40,869 --> 01:22:43,702
You can drink your last few hours away
on a beach,

711
01:22:43,809 --> 01:22:46,972
which by the way, is not a bad idea

712
01:22:48,453 --> 01:22:51,251
or you can follow me one last time.

713
01:23:01,716 --> 01:23:04,844
We got to make the best use
of our resources.

714
01:23:04,957 --> 01:23:08,654
We got to have a strict...
Listen to me, damn it!

715
01:23:09,233 --> 01:23:12,498
He doesn't understand tactics.
You got to explain to him.

716
01:23:12,607 --> 01:23:15,940
Look, we can't just run around hollering

717
01:23:16,049 --> 01:23:19,348
and throwing spears and
shooting arrows at the damn thing.

718
01:23:19,456 --> 01:23:23,586
We got to draw them out of there
onto open ground

719
01:23:23,699 --> 01:23:27,100
where we can surround them,
attack them on all sides.

720
01:23:27,207 --> 01:23:29,334
Flank them. Explain to him.

721
01:23:32,953 --> 01:23:36,252
He said he's not going to let you
lead his people.

722
01:23:46,417 --> 01:23:48,112
What's he saying?

723
01:23:49,791 --> 01:23:51,816
He's saying they need to
open their hearts

724
01:23:51,929 --> 01:23:55,228
and see in you what he has seen.

725
01:23:59,514 --> 01:24:02,312
That his parents
died in the Mexican War

726
01:24:03,021 --> 01:24:05,785
and you took him in
when he was only a boy.

727
01:24:08,567 --> 01:24:10,660
That you gave him purpose.

728
01:24:11,474 --> 01:24:16,036
Taught him how to take care of himself
even though you were not blood.

729
01:24:21,062 --> 01:24:25,362
That you despise battle
but would never run from it.

730
01:24:27,477 --> 01:24:31,208
That you're a fierce warrior
worthy of any fight.

731
01:24:50,395 --> 01:24:51,828
He says if you're such a great warrior,

732
01:24:51,932 --> 01:24:54,833
why do you only have a man and a boy
to follow you into battle?

733
01:25:30,318 --> 01:25:33,151
Dog! Dog!

734
01:25:34,996 --> 01:25:36,293
Boy!

735
01:25:36,399 --> 01:25:37,696
How are you?

736
01:25:49,596 --> 01:25:51,826
Hot damn.

737
01:25:52,402 --> 01:25:54,666
Ready to get your son back?

738
01:27:17,795 --> 01:27:19,854
Give me that. Okay.

739
01:27:28,151 --> 01:27:29,618
Matches.

740
01:27:40,813 --> 01:27:43,577
I don't have any more matches.
We're gonna have to go down.

741
01:27:43,687 --> 01:27:45,052
I don't know what we're going to do.

742
01:27:52,707 --> 01:27:54,766
Go. Go!

743
01:28:08,276 --> 01:28:09,436
Go. Go!

744
01:28:49,536 --> 01:28:51,265
I think we destroyed it.

745
01:29:03,601 --> 01:29:05,535
Demons are coming out.

746
01:29:09,414 --> 01:29:11,575
Take this. Go up where I showed you.

747
01:29:11,686 --> 01:29:13,415
- You see our people, wave your arms.
- Yes, sir.

748
01:29:13,524 --> 01:29:15,424
Move out!

749
01:29:28,825 --> 01:29:30,224
Good job.

750
01:29:30,328 --> 01:29:33,661
If our people are in there,
I'll get them out.

751
01:29:33,769 --> 01:29:34,997
Godspeed.

752
01:29:36,476 --> 01:29:37,773
Let's get them!

753
01:30:51,044 --> 01:30:53,638
This is how they get the gold out.

754
01:31:18,005 --> 01:31:19,438
They're not going down!

755
01:31:19,542 --> 01:31:22,978
They will!
Keep at it till we get our people out!

756
01:32:25,057 --> 01:32:26,183
Doc!

757
01:32:26,928 --> 01:32:28,555
Doc, get down here!

758
01:32:31,738 --> 01:32:32,864
Jesus.

759
01:32:35,747 --> 01:32:36,873
Doc!

760
01:32:38,186 --> 01:32:39,710
Did we get one?

761
01:32:41,493 --> 01:32:43,154
Yeah, we got one.

762
01:32:45,002 --> 01:32:49,735
I always dreamed of riding into battle
with you.

763
01:32:52,786 --> 01:32:55,812
I always dreamed
of having a son like you.

764
01:32:59,434 --> 01:33:00,492
Go.

765
01:33:01,272 --> 01:33:02,569
Get Percy.

766
01:33:03,477 --> 01:33:04,944
Get your son.

767
01:34:33,914 --> 01:34:35,472
Don't look into the light.

768
01:35:11,366 --> 01:35:13,994
- I told you not to look into the light.
- Yeah, right.

769
01:35:33,783 --> 01:35:35,546
How long are they gonna be like this?

770
01:35:35,654 --> 01:35:37,451
Each one's different.

771
01:35:42,403 --> 01:35:43,461
Hold them off.

772
01:35:43,572 --> 01:35:45,472
You'd better hurry.

773
01:36:26,168 --> 01:36:28,636
There's more of them coming!

774
01:37:03,486 --> 01:37:04,783
Go!

775
01:37:29,311 --> 01:37:30,835
Everybody's out.

776
01:37:31,483 --> 01:37:32,814
Right.

777
01:37:34,222 --> 01:37:36,690
Hey! Where are you going?

778
01:37:37,263 --> 01:37:39,857
It's this way!

779
01:38:29,147 --> 01:38:30,239
Go. Go!

780
01:40:06,266 --> 01:40:08,393
What the hell are you doing?
We have to get out of here!

781
01:40:08,504 --> 01:40:09,698
No!

782
01:40:10,309 --> 01:40:12,334
I came here to destroy that thing.

783
01:40:12,447 --> 01:40:13,436
How?

784
01:40:13,550 --> 01:40:15,643
With the bracelet. Take it off.

785
01:40:15,989 --> 01:40:17,718
Wait, I can't take it off.

786
01:40:17,826 --> 01:40:19,453
Yes, you can. You can control it.

787
01:40:19,563 --> 01:40:22,157
- How?
- Same way you shoot it. With your mind.

788
01:40:23,705 --> 01:40:25,866
You have to stop thinking.

789
01:40:36,969 --> 01:40:38,266
This isn't working.

790
01:40:54,075 --> 01:40:55,542
It fell off.

791
01:41:05,100 --> 01:41:08,228
If I can get it to its core,
I can stop them.

792
01:41:10,879 --> 01:41:12,870
Let's go.

793
01:41:23,976 --> 01:41:25,273
Take this.

794
01:41:51,537 --> 01:41:52,697
Throw it!

795
01:41:57,919 --> 01:41:59,910
- Good-bye, Jake.
- What?

796
01:42:01,360 --> 01:42:03,555
Wait! Ella!

797
01:42:05,336 --> 01:42:06,564
No!

798
01:43:06,842 --> 01:43:08,833
I see them! I see them!

799
01:43:08,946 --> 01:43:10,880
They got out.
They're coming out the other side!

800
01:43:10,984 --> 01:43:12,144
You see Percy?

801
01:43:16,330 --> 01:43:17,319
Yeah, I see him!

802
01:43:17,432 --> 01:43:18,922
What about Jake and Ella?

803
01:43:19,504 --> 01:43:21,631
No. They're not there.

804
01:46:21,047 --> 01:46:22,639
You all right, old man?

805
01:46:32,272 --> 01:46:35,207
- Where's the girl?
- She's still inside.

806
01:46:41,360 --> 01:46:42,486
Go!

807
01:49:06,823 --> 01:49:07,881
Grandpa!

808
01:49:08,927 --> 01:49:10,224
It's me.

809
01:49:12,234 --> 01:49:13,360
Emmett.

810
01:49:13,471 --> 01:49:14,768
Emmett.

811
01:49:20,854 --> 01:49:22,651
You're all grown up.

812
01:49:30,375 --> 01:49:31,899
Percy.

813
01:49:36,689 --> 01:49:38,919
Don't you remember me, boy?

814
01:49:39,863 --> 01:49:44,061
I'm sorry. I don't remember much.

815
01:49:44,909 --> 01:49:46,536
I'm your father.

816
01:49:47,982 --> 01:49:49,506
Pa.

817
01:49:59,876 --> 01:50:02,242
Do you remember me?

818
01:50:15,544 --> 01:50:19,207
I thought you were dead.
I thought you were dead.

819
01:52:01,618 --> 01:52:04,644
All this gold's
gonna make things different.

820
01:52:05,092 --> 01:52:08,823
We're gonna have
a railroad in here soon.

821
01:52:08,934 --> 01:52:11,528
That'll change the cattle business.

822
01:52:13,778 --> 01:52:16,975
Run these ledgers
back to the bank for me, will you?

823
01:52:17,086 --> 01:52:19,486
Tell them I need some new checks.

824
01:52:20,393 --> 01:52:21,485
Okay.

825
01:52:23,500 --> 01:52:27,596
I want the new ones to read
"Dolarhyde and Son."

826
01:52:30,616 --> 01:52:34,746
- That sound good to you?
- Yes. Yes, sir.

827
01:52:46,652 --> 01:52:49,519
- John.
- Woodrow.

828
01:52:50,963 --> 01:52:54,524
It appears our town
is about to get a whole lot bigger.

829
01:52:59,716 --> 01:53:02,310
You weren't gonna leave
without saying good-bye, were you?

830
01:53:06,130 --> 01:53:07,893
I'm a wanted man.

831
01:53:08,836 --> 01:53:12,431
I could have sworn I saw
Jake Lonergan die in those caves,

832
01:53:12,544 --> 01:53:13,977
didn't you, Sheriff?

833
01:53:14,081 --> 01:53:15,708
Damn shame.

834
01:53:15,818 --> 01:53:18,048
I was looking forward
to hanging him myself.

835
01:53:20,029 --> 01:53:21,758
I could use a good man around here.

836
01:53:21,866 --> 01:53:23,663
Yes, you could.

837
01:53:29,115 --> 01:53:30,343
Jake.

838
01:53:32,690 --> 01:53:34,715
She's in a better place.

839
01:53:38,537 --> 01:53:40,061
I'll see you around, Colonel.

840
01:53:40,111 --> 01:53:44,661
